{"user": "where did I go wrong?", "user_ts": "2026-08-05T17:19:03.077638+00:00", "assistant": "From this final board, Black lost **19\u201345**. The big issue is visible:\n\n- White owns **3 corners**: **a1, h1, a8**. Black only has **h8**.\n- White also has most of the **top edge and left edge**, which become very hard/impossible to flip.\n- Your Black discs are mostly clustered on the right/bottom, but they don\u2019t outweigh White\u2019s stable corners/edges.\n\nSo you probably went wrong by:\n1. **Giving White corner access** \u2014 often by playing squares next to empty corners.\n2. **Chasing flips** instead of asking \u201cdoes this let White take a corner or edge?\u201d\n3. **Letting White keep mobility** while your choices got limited.\n\nRule of thumb for next game: in the endgame, a move that flips 1 disc but wins/denies a corner is usually better than a move that flips 6 but hands over a corner.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-05T17:19:14.121883+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-05T17:19:17.771345+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Neutral Feedback"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority"