{"user": "okay so always go for the corners", "user_ts": "2026-08-05T17:20:49.734846+00:00", "assistant": "Almost \u2014 **take a corner when you can**, because corners are permanent.\n\nBut don\u2019t play *near* an empty corner carelessly:\n\n- **Good:** taking **a1 / h1 / a8 / h8**\n- **Dangerous:** playing next to an empty corner, like **b1, a2, b2** near **a1**, because it may let White take the corner.\n\nSo the rule is:\n\n**\u201cCorners are great \u2014 but don\u2019t hand them to White.\u201d**\n\nIn your shown board the game is already over: **Black 19, White 45**. White\u2019s corners/edges were the big difference.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-05T17:20:57.277744+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-05T17:20:59.275343+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Conversational Acknowledgment": 2}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Conversational Acknowledgment": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 1, "Neutral Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Neutral Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes